            <div xml:id="d1055">

                <pb facs="1198" n="1054" xml:id="pg1054"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">462.00R296/2783a: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Chargé in France</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Armour</hi>)</head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Paraphrase]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1929-04-13T18:00:00-05:00">April 13, 1929—6
                    p.m.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p>109. For Young.</p>
                <p>Press carries report that figures on reparations will be given out Monday.
                    Complete statement of this Government’s position will be telegraphed you
                    tomorrow, and it is hoped that there may be no publicity until after you have
                    had opportunity to consider statement. I may add that Mr. Wilson’s letter of
                    April 12 to you correctly states position of this Government respecting mixed
                    claims and Army costs.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Stimson</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
